        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fields, In Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "class P {",
            "  a = 1        // before constructor body",
            "  #secret = 2  // real per-instance slot",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Instance fields initialize in source order",
            "All of them run before the constructor statements",
            "`#x` is unreachable via the chain or reflection"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Memory Per Method",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Style",
            "Functions allocated"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "prototype method",
              "1 per class"
            ],
            [
              "factory / closure",
              "1 per instance"
            ],
            [
              "arrow class field",
              "1 per instance"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Property Access Speed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An own property is the fastest read",
            "Each chain hop adds work on a miss",
            "Inline caches and hidden classes hide most of it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Killing The Cache"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Object.setPrototypeOf(o, p)  // classic deopt",
            "o.lateField = 1              // shape change",
            "// both go megamorphic in hot code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Privacy Options"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Privacy",
            "Sharing"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "closure",
              "true, cheap",
              "per instance"
            ],
            [
              "`#private`",
              "true",
              "prototype methods"
            ],
            [
              "`_name`",
              "none",
              "prototype methods"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What class Buys"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`extends`, `super`, static inheritance",
            "Better stack traces and devtools output",
            "One obvious shape for entities with identity"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Factories Buy"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mixins and object spread compose freely",
            "JS has one `[[Prototype]]` — no multiple inheritance",
            "`Object.assign(C.prototype, behavior)` copies, no link",
            "Copied mixins never see later updates"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Depth And Freezing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "4+ level chains hurt speed and comprehension",
            "Prefer composition over deep inheritance",
            "`Object.freeze(C.prototype)` locks shared methods",
            "Frozen: monkey-patching fails silently in sloppy mode"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Choosing",
          "text": "`class` for entities with identity and inheritance. Factories and closures for stateful units and privacy. Plain objects plus functions for data."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "`class` Desugared (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lost Receivers",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "arr.forEach(this.handler)             // lost",
            "arr.forEach(this.handler.bind(this))  // fix",
            "arr.forEach(x => this.handler(x))     // or fix"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Common Mistakes and Gotchas",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "More Lost-this Shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`setTimeout(obj.method, 0)` drops the receiver",
            "Browsers then set timer `this` to `window`",
            "Arrow as prototype/object method: module or window",
            "Bare-called class method: TypeError, bodies are strict",
            "`boundFn.call(other)` never rebinds"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shared Mutable State"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Dog.prototype.toys = []   // ONE array, shared",
            "a.toys.push('ball')",
            "b.toys                    // ['ball'] — oops"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Arrays and objects belong in the constructor body",
            "`this.toys = []` gives each instance its own"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Replacing The Prototype"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`C.prototype = {...}` wipes `constructor`",
            "Instances made earlier still point at the OLD object",
            "They never see any of the new methods"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Untrusted Keys"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "merge({}, JSON.parse(body))  // \"__proto__\" key",
            "// mutates Object.prototype globally",
            "const t = Object.create(null)  // safe target"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reject `__proto__` and `constructor.prototype` keys",
            "Or merge into a null-prototype target"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Enumeration And Identity"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Common Mistakes and Gotchas (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`for...in` picks up a polluted Object.prototype",
            "Guard with `Object.hasOwn`, or use `Object.keys`",
            "`instanceof` fails across realms: iframes, workers, vm",
            "Use `Array.isArray` or `Symbol.hasInstance` instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "null Has No Prototype"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "typeof null          // 'object' — old bug",
            "[].toString.call(null) // [object Null]",
            "null.x               // TypeError"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Derived Constructors"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Forgetting `super()`: ReferenceError, not undefined",
            "Using `this` before `super()`: same error",
            "`super()` is what creates `this` in the first place"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Whole Model",
          "text": "Objects delegate property lookups up a chain of objects, and functions receive `this` from how they are called."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Decision Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
